# Project Overview — Engineering Domain

The Engineering domain covers all build engineering, hardening, integration, and implementation patterns for the Omega Engine. This includes the build system, provider fabric, memory store, entity registry, and all core infrastructure.

## Scope
- Build system (pyproject.toml, install.sh, Makefile)
- Provider fabric (ModelGateway, backends, provider priority)
- Memory store (sqlite-vec, hybrid search, MemoryStore)
- Entity registry (YAML-backed CRUD, workspaces)
- Hivemind coordination (awareness, handoffs, locks)
- Hardening (ResourceGuard, OOMProtector, HealthMonitor)
- Deployment (Podman, systemd, secrets)

## Key Principles
1. **Local-first** — Cloud is fallback only
2. **Single source of truth** — pyproject.toml, providers.yaml, models.yaml
3. **Atomic changes** — One ticket = one PR = one semantic change
4. **Defense in depth** — M1, M7, M8, M9, M23 mandates
5. **Resource management** — Single local slot, OOMProtector, HealthMonitor

## Current State (2026-08-19)
- Phase C hardening COMPLETE (C-0 through C-11)
- PUBLIC-DEBUT-01 in progress (Blocker B → INST-1 → PUB-1 → DEL-1)
- sqlite-vec = core vector store (zero-dependency)
- Qdrant = optional WAD adapter (post-debut)
- Fleet = 14 agents (M10 cap)